name issue_390_cross_join_seed15
describe issue_204_cross_traffic_join on seed 15: when the 2 Mbps cross traffic and the call's packets reach the full 300 ms queue in the same millisecond, the cross traffic goes first, as in sm_compare, so the call takes its share of the drops and its rate falls below the free 1 Mbps after the second cut (#390)
# main before the fix: the test bench put the call's packets of a tick ahead of the cross traffic, so the cross traffic
# took the drop-tail drops (#392's traces: 8-15 % of ours dropped in 10.4-11.4 s against 15-19 % of libwebrtc's, on
# all four seeds traced). Ours kept about 1.13 Mbps through the second after the second cut, the queue stayed full,
# and the call stuck above capacity: 15 freezes, 5434 ms. Seeds 1-80 on main: 9 stuck (>= 10 freezes), mean 4.75
# freezes. libwebrtc: 0 of 80 stuck, mean 2.76, at most 9 on one seed (#389, compare_seeds 80).
# With the fix, this seed: 4 freezes, 1886 ms. Seeds 1-80: 3 stuck (seeds 5, 62, 76), mean 3.27.
# Target (issue #390): stuck-mode share 0 of 80, as libwebrtc.
duration 40s
seed 15
at 0s capacity=3000kbps delay=40ms queue=300ms
at 10s cross=2000kbps
at 25s cross=0kbps
expect video.freeze_count <= 9
expect video.freeze_total_ms < 3000
# #556 + #549: seed 15 at 286.8; libwebrtc seed 15 292.8, worst 295.3 (tight rule, cap).
expect cc.queue_p95_ms < 295
